cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ARGOS: Reinforcement Learning-Driven Multidimensional Elasticity for Service Orchestration in the Computing Continuum"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jamateosb/ARGOS"
abstract: >-
  ARGOS (Adaptive Reinforcement Learning-Driven Governance for Orchestrated
  Services) is an orchestrator for analytics services on heterogeneous
  computing-continuum nodes. It admits requests with accepted ranges for
  coverage, sample, and freshness, and adapts each admitted request within
  those ranges under observed resource pressure, using learned (Q-learning,
  DQN, PPO) or non-learning controllers. The repository contains the source
  code, the evaluation configuration and scripts, the result tables, and the
  code that generates every figure.
keywords:
  - computing continuum
  - multidimensional elasticity
  - reinforcement learning
  - service orchestration
  - admission control
  - edge computing
